# Make Intel RAPL energy counters world-readable.
#
# /sys/class/powercap/intel-rapl:0/energy_uj ships as mode 0400 root:root,
# so the quickshell System panel cannot read package power as a normal user.
# It is the substitute for CPU voltage, which this hardware exposes no
# sensor for at all (see plugins/bar/widgets/system-stats.sh).
#
# The counter was restricted upstream because a high-frequency reader can
# mount a side-channel attack recovering AES keys (CVE-2020-8694, "PLATYPUS").
# Granting read here is a deliberate, local trade for a watts readout on a
# single-user laptop. If that is not a trade you want, delete this rule:
# the panel already handles the counter being unreadable and simply reports
# package power as unavailable.
SUBSYSTEM=="powercap", ACTION=="add", RUN+="/bin/chmod -R a+r /sys/devices/virtual/powercap"
